//RS /// Invoke a retained route callback on an HTTP worker and resolve its result
//RS /// while the worker still holds the resident runtime.
//RS ///
//RS /// Workers are raw OS threads: `try_with_http_jet_runtime_at` pins the
//RS /// published runtime onto the thread only for the closure it runs, so every
//RS /// heap read of the callback's result — unpacking the `Result`, cloning the
//RS /// page or text it names — has to happen inside that same closure.  Reading
//RS /// after it returns runs with no runtime and aborts the request.
